SLLM patch 10 (phase2-qmm32, phase2-qmm32b): qmm with one accumulation order for every row count. kernel_sllm_qmm_ks
(kernels/qmm.metal) takes every Q4_0 / Q4_1 mat-mul with N >= 2 src1 rows (N = 1 stays on ggml's mat-vec): one
threadgroup per 32 weight rows x 16 or 32 token rows (bitwise the same per-row results), its 4 or 8 simdgroups split K
inside the threadgroup (contiguous or interleaved slices) and sum their partials in threadgroup memory, so there is no
grid split-K scratch and no reduce dispatch; the weights are matmul2d's left operand, whose register layout gives each
lane 4-byte runs of a row; above 64 rows two 32-row tiles share a threadgroup (and its activation reads), with the
same per-row arithmetic, so prefill chunks are not slower than ggml's mul_mm (phase2-qmm32b). kernel_sllm_qmm_q6p takes Q6_K (the LM heads, 2..128 rows) with the K
order permuted inside each 32-K chunk so every lane loads whole words of ql/qh (activations staged as half in the same
order). ggml-metal-qmm.{h,m}: plan field ks, args field pad renamed flags (same layout), SLLM_QMM32 / SLLM_QMM32_G /
SLLM_QMM32_IL / SLLM_QMM32_Q6, the self-test extended to both kernels (with a bitwise row-count check), status
field "qmm32".
Against llama.cpp b11669 (source tarball 620d222) after patches 0001..0009, applied with patch -p1 in ggml/.
